<title>UK: Energy Group to sell assets to Lehman.</title>
<headline>Energy Group to sell assets to Lehman.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Energy Group announced on Friday it was planning to sell select assets of Citizens Power LLC to Lehman Brothers Holdings Inc.</p>
<p>Citizens Power, the country's fifth largest power marketing firm, is a subsidiary of the Energy Group.  </p>
<p>Energy Group faces a $9.6 billion take-over offer from U.S. energy group PacifiCorp. Energy said it was selling those assets that were subject to jurisdiction under the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission.</p>
<p>The company did not announce the consideration of the transaction.</p>
<p>The sale of the assets was subject to PacifiCorp's successful completion of the tender offer for Energy Group's shares.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4366</p>
